My Sunday morning in the flat is very quiet.
In the afternoon, I open my laptop.
In Mexico it is eight hours earlier, so it is just breakfast time there.
I call my family by video.
My parents, my sister Sofia and my brother Diego are sitting at the table.
In the background, our dog Lola barks happily.
"Hello everyone!" I call out and wave.
"How are you doing, Maya?" my mother asks immediately.
I tell them about my week.
"On Thursday I played badminton against Lena," I say.
"It was very hot in the hall, but we had a lot of fun."
Diego laughs and asks, "Did you win?"
"That is a secret," I answer with a smile.
Then I talk about my Saturday evening.
"I cooked a big meal for my neighbour Sabine last night."
"I even specifically bought the right spices!"
Sofia smiles and says, "She definitely thought our family recipe was great."
"Yes, she did," I say and nod.
"And what else are you doing today on this beautiful Sunday?"
We talk comfortably for quite a while longer about their day.
